From a497dda15150881d7eacbd850bcd4b01c220b082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:25:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: sparx5: give each leak group its own rate
Organization: Wires

The leak groups of a layer are set up from the rate of the group with
the layer's index: on LAN969x layer 0's four groups all serve
655 Mbit/s, so a faster queue shaper is refused, and layer 2's all
serve 6.5 Gbit/s, so a slow port shaper gets a coarse resolution.

Index the rate table by the group.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <joachim.wiberg@wires.se>
Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
index a38c98bdc4e7..daec69c79a54 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.c
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@ static int sparx5_leak_groups_init(struct sparx5 *sparx5)
 		layer = &layers[i];
 		for (ii = 0; ii < SPX5_HSCH_LEAK_GRP_CNT; ii++) {
 			lg = &layer->leak_groups[ii];
-			lg->max_rate = ops->get_hsch_max_group_rate(i);
+			lg->max_rate = ops->get_hsch_max_group_rate(ii);
 
 			/* Calculate the leak time in us, to serve a maximum
 			 * rate of 'max_rate' for this group
